From 179d0ca356358a88dcf91e6885d8e6cf3125a644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KyeYongChoo <163633375+KyeYongChoo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:20:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add dev_set_deck action and run.act_id

dev_set_deck replaces the master deck with an exact list of cards,
including upgrades and enchantments. The dev console's upgrade/enchant
commands only touch the combat hand, so there was no way to set up a
test fight's deck with those. Every entry is validated before the deck
is touched; the swap reuses the console commands' own game calls.

run.act_id exposes which act model the current act rolled (e.g.
OVERGROWTH vs UNDERDOCKS), which run.act's index alone can't tell apart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
